From: DiffusionGemma/Xe2 backend investigation
Subject: [GIST/UNVERIFIED] sdpa micro-kernel: add sliding-window key lower bound (k0start)

WHAT / WHY
----------
oneDNN's micro SDPA kernel (src/gpu/intel/sdpa/micro.cl) already trims the
*upper* key range for causal masks via `k0end` (FlashAttention-style block
skipping). It has NO *lower* key bound: the K-loop always starts at key 0.

Gemma3/Gemma4 (and DiffusionGemma) use HYBRID attention: most layers are
`sliding_attention` (local window W), interleaved with a few `full_attention`
layers. Today the only way to run a sliding-window layer through this kernel is
to pass the window as an additive `attn_mask` buffer (-inf outside the band).
That is functionally correct but computes the ENTIRE lower key range and masks
it: O(seq * k0end) work instead of SWA's O(seq * W).

This patch adds a symmetric `k0start` lower bound so out-of-window key blocks
are skipped entirely, mirroring the existing `k0end` logic.

STATUS: ILLUSTRATIVE / UNVERIFIED. This shows the .cl-side change only. It has
NOT been compiled, run, or benchmarked. See "VERIFICATION REQUIRED" below.
The host-side plumbing (descriptor field + kernel defines + dispatch gating) is
NOT included here and is required for this to do anything.

ASSUMPTIONS TO CHECK
--------------------
* `ugemm_kq(..., k0end, ..., d, k0, 0, 0, ...)` uses `k0` as the K row offset
  (micro.cl:816-817), so changing only the loop start is sufficient for the
  GEMM to address the correct keys — no K base-pointer rebasing needed for the
  matmul itself.
* `first` (micro.cl:770 -> used at :984) gates online-softmax accumulator init;
  it must become `(k0 == k0start)`, else the first in-window block wrongly
  rescales the accumulator.
* The first-K prefetch (micro.cl:669-682) still prefetches from row 0; with
  k0start>0 it warms a skipped tile. Correctness-neutral, perf-suboptimal —
  flagged as a TODO, not fixed here.
* The `if (k0end > 0)` setup/epilogue guards (628,647,670,713,735,1145,1207)
  assume "any work => start at 0". With windowing the precise predicate is
  `k0end > k0start`; left as-is here because in SWA every valid query attends at
  least itself so k0end > k0start always holds. Revisit for fully-masked rows.

--- a/src/gpu/intel/sdpa/micro.cl
+++ b/src/gpu/intel/sdpa/micro.cl
@@ -536,6 +536,10 @@
     /* Calculate the number of keys to process */
     int k0end = k;
+    /* Lower bound on keys to process. 0 for full/causal attention; raised for
+     * sliding-window (local) attention so out-of-window key blocks are skipped
+     * entirely instead of being computed and then masked to -inf. */
+    int k0start = 0;
 #if WITH_CAUSAL_MASK
     if (attn_mask_type == ATTN_MASK_TOP_LEFT) {
         k0end = min(k, (int)(wg_j0 + ugemm_kq_wg_tile_n));
         if (q == 1) k0end = 1;
     } else {
         k0end = min(k, (int)(wg_j0 + ugemm_kq_wg_tile_n) - (q - k));
     }
 #endif
+#if WITH_SLIDING_WINDOW
+    /* Lowest key any query in this workgroup tile attends:
+     *   query rows in tile = [wg_j0, wg_j0 + ugemm_kq_wg_tile_n)
+     *   each query q attends keys in (q - SLIDING_WINDOW, q]
+     * Use the tile's minimum query row (wg_j0) and align DOWN to the K block
+     * size so GEMM tiling stays aligned. The (q - k) shift mirrors the
+     * bottom_right branch of the k0end computation above. */
+    int win_lo = (int)wg_j0 - (int)SLIDING_WINDOW + 1;
+#if WITH_CAUSAL_MASK
+    if (attn_mask_type != ATTN_MASK_TOP_LEFT) win_lo -= (q - k);
+#endif
+    k0start = max(0, win_lo);
+    k0start = (k0start / ugemm_kq_wg_tile_m) * ugemm_kq_wg_tile_m;
+#endif

     /* Leading dimension for matrices */
     uint ldk = TRANSPOSE_K ? KEY_S3 : KEY_S2;
@@ -766,8 +770,8 @@
     /* Main loop over key blocks */
-    for (int k0 = 0; k0 < k0end; k0 += ugemm_kq_wg_tile_m) {
-        bool first = (k0 == 0);
+    for (int k0 = k0start; k0 < k0end; k0 += ugemm_kq_wg_tile_m) {
+        bool first = (k0 == k0start);
         int knext = k0 + ugemm_kq_wg_tile_m;
         bool last = (knext >= k0end);


REQUIRED HOST-SIDE PLUMBING (not in this gist; sketch only)
-----------------------------------------------------------
1. src/common/sdpa_types.hpp : add `dim_t sliding_window {};` to sdpa_desc_t
   (0 = disabled), plus an accessor.
2. src/gpu/intel/sdpa/micro.cpp : when sliding_window > 0, emit kernel defines
   `-DWITH_SLIDING_WINDOW=1 -DSLIDING_WINDOW=<W>` alongside the existing
   WITH_CAUSAL_MASK / attn_mask_type defines; gate dispatch/config as needed.
3. Plumb sliding_window from the Graph API SDP partition (or the internal PD
   creation path) down into sdpa_desc_t.
4. Decide interaction with attn_mask buffer: with a real k0start, the additive
   band mask for the *skipped* region is no longer needed; the in-window
   remainder edges may still need masking.

VERIFICATION REQUIRED (the hypothesis this patch rests on)
----------------------------------------------------------
The CLAIM is: "for Gemma sliding layers on long sequences, mask-buffer SWA on
the current kernel pays full lower-range compute, and k0start recovers SWA's
O(seq*W) cost." This is UNPROVEN. Before relying on it:

A. CORRECTNESS: build oneDNN with the full plumbing, run sdpa with a window and
   compare outputs against (a) the dense reference (ref.cl) with an equivalent
   additive band mask, and (b) a PyTorch/vLLM SWA reference. Bit-for-bit class
   match within tolerance.

B. PERF / NECESSITY: benchmark the CURRENT kernel (window via additive mask, no
   k0start) vs the PATCHED kernel, sweeping sequence length (e.g. 512 ... 32k)
   at fixed window W. Confirm:
     - current kernel runtime scales ~O(seq) per query (i.e. O(seq^2) total) —
       i.e. it does NOT already cap work at the window, and
     - patched kernel runtime flattens to ~O(W) per query for seq >> W.
   If the current kernel already plateaus (e.g. a higher layer caps k0end, or
   the mask makes the GEMM cheap enough), THIS PATCH IS UNNECESSARY and should
   be dropped. Short canvases / short contexts likely see no benefit.

C. Confirm Xe2 specifically: measure on the actual Xe2 dGPU target, not just
   functional emulation, since the win is bandwidth/EU-occupancy dependent.
